# Pay UI build artifact. Produced by the pay repo, not here: the Dockerfile
# copies /srv out of ${PAY_IMAGE} (ghcr.io/hanzoai/pay) before the Go build.
# Only .gitkeep is tracked so go:embed resolves on a fresh clone.
checkout/ui/dist/*
!checkout/ui/dist/.gitkeep

# Billing admin UI build artifact. Produced by the billing repo, not here: the
# Dockerfile copies /public out of ${BILLING_IMAGE} (ghcr.io/hanzoai/billing)
# before the Go build. Only .gitkeep is tracked so go:embed resolves on a
# fresh clone.
billing/ui/dist/*
!billing/ui/dist/.gitkeep

# Commerce admin build artifact. The source of truth is app/admin; the ONLY
# producer is scripts/sync-admin-ui.sh copying app/admin/out here, run by
# Dockerfile's admin-build stage before the Go build. It was tracked
# content until now, which is exactly why it went stale: the committed bundle
# was a retired Vite SPA while app/admin had moved on. Only .gitkeep is tracked
# so go:embed resolves on a fresh clone. The admin mount is standalone-only
# (commerce.go registers it under `if !embedded`), so the library consumer —
# hanzoai/cloud's unified binary — never serves it and loses nothing.
ui/dist/*
!ui/dist/.gitkeep

# hanzoai/plans is the SOT; scripts/fetch-plans.sh refreshes these at build.
# BUT the two files below are go:embed'd (api/billing/plans.go), so they MUST be
# committed: a Go module cannot embed a gitignored file, and cloud consumes
# commerce AS A LIBRARY (the unified binary) where the module zip is all there is
# — omitting them broke every downstream build from v1.42.30 (0de841321) on. The
# rest of plans/ stays fetched/untracked.
api/billing/plans/*
!api/billing/plans/dns.json
!api/billing/plans/subscription.json
/backfill-events
app/admin/out/

# turbo writes its build cache at the repo root; app/.gitignore only covers app/.turbo.
.turbo/
